  "summary": "18 published single-cell and spatial transcriptomics items on immune and stromal compartments; gut microbiota is addressed in only a few reviews.",
  "synthesis": "Eighteen published items, with no preprints, code, or industry records. Few address gut microbial communities directly: the Journal of Allergy review covers microbiome niches in inflammatory skin disease, the TIPS review addresses perianal fistulizing Crohn's disease, and the PSC review integrates microbiome with bile acid metabolism and Th17 responses. The bulk applies single-cell and spatial transcriptomics to immune and stromal compartments across autoimmune, infectious, intestinal, and hepatic settings. Representative examples include CD47hi fibroblasts and SIRPAhi macrophages in Crohn's intestinal fibrosis, Ms4a6c+ macrophages in radiation proctitis, and a biliary atresia liver atlas with CXCL12-CXCR4 signaling. The rise ratio of 3.1 with zero 7-day star gain describes observed volume only; the items do not establish a cause for the increase.",
